(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the differential equation of motion for a damped harmonic oscillator with viscous resistance. Obtain the auxiliary characteristic equation and classify the three distinct regimes of damping.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Model and Force Balance:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider a particle or structural mass m attached to an elastic restoring spring of stiffness) Tj
T*
(   k and experiencing a viscous damping force proportional to velocity:) Tj
T*
(   * Restoring force: F_s = - k * x.) Tj
T*
(   * Damping resistance: F_d = - b * \(dx / dt\), where b is the damping coefficient \(N*s/m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Applying Newton's Second Law: m * \(d^2x / dt^2\) = F_s + F_d = - k * x - b * \(dx / dt\).) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging into standard form:) Tj
T*
(   m * \(d^2x / dt^2\) + b * \(dx / dt\) + k * x = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Dividing by m and defining natural angular frequency omega_0 = sqrt\(k / m\) and damping factor) Tj
T*
(   2*beta = b / m \(or beta = b / 2m\):) Tj
T*
(   d^2x / dt^2 + 2*beta * \(dx / dt\) + omega_0^2 * x = 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Characteristic Equation and Roots:) Tj
T*
(   - Assume trial solution x\(t\) = exp\(r * t\). Substituting into the differential equation:) Tj
T*
(   r^2 + 2*beta * r + omega_0^2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Solving the quadratic characteristic equation:) Tj
T*
(   r = - beta +- sqrt\( beta^2 - omega_0^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Classification of Damping Regimes:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Overdamped Case \(beta > omega_0, b > 2*sqrt\(k*m\)\):) Tj
T*
(   * The discriminant is positive; roots r1, r2 are real, distinct, and negative.) Tj
T*
(   * Solution: x\(t\) = C1 * exp\(r1*t\) + C2 * exp\(r2*t\).) Tj
T*
(   * Motion is non-oscillatory \(deadbeat\); system returns sluggishly to equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Critically Damped Case \(beta = omega_0, b = 2*sqrt\(k*m\)\):) Tj
T*
(   * The discriminant is zero; roots are real, equal, and negative: r1 = r2 = - beta.) Tj
T*
(   * Solution: x\(t\) = \( C1 + C2 * t \) * exp\( - beta * t \).) Tj
T*
(   * The system returns to equilibrium in the minimum possible time without any oscillation.) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) Underdamped Case \(beta < omega_0, b < 2*sqrt\(k*m\)\):) Tj
T*
(   * The discriminant is negative; roots are complex conjugates: r = - beta +- i * omega_d, where) Tj
T*
(   omega_d = sqrt\(omega_0^2 - beta^2\).) Tj
T*
(   * Solution: x\(t\) = A_0 * exp\( - beta * t \) * cos\( omega_d * t + phi \).) Tj
T*
(   * Motion is oscillatory with exponentially decaying amplitude.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
