/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the complete displacement solution for an underdamped harmonic oscillator. Define logarithmic decrement, relaxation time, and Quality factor Q.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Underdamped Differential Equation and Solution:) Tj
T*
(   - For beta < omega_0, the characteristic roots are r = - beta +- i * omega_d, where omega_d =) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\( omega_0^2 - beta^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - The general displacement solution is:) Tj
T*
(   x\(t\) = A_0 * exp\( - beta * t \) * cos\( omega_d * t - phi \),) Tj
T*
(   where A_0 is initial amplitude and phi is phase constant determined by initial conditions.) Tj
T*
(   - The period of damped oscillation is T_d = 2 * pi / omega_d = 2 * pi / sqrt\( omega_0^2 -) Tj
T*
(   beta^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Logarithmic Decrement \(delta\):) Tj
T*
ET

