(   - Let x_n and x_{n+1} be successive displacement peaks occurring at times t_n and t_n + T_d.) Tj
T*
(   - The ratio of successive peak amplitudes is:) Tj
T*
(   x_n / x_{n+1} = [ A_0 * exp\(- beta * t_n\) ] / [ A_0 * exp\(- beta * \(t_n + T_d\)\) ] = exp\( beta *) Tj
T*
(   T_d \).) Tj
T*
(   - The logarithmic decrement delta is defined as the natural logarithm of this amplitude ratio:) Tj
T*
(   delta = ln\( x_n / x_{n+1} \) = beta * T_d = \(2 * pi * beta\) / omega_d.) Tj
T*
(   - For light damping \(beta << omega_0, omega_d ~= omega_0\): delta ~= 2 * pi * beta / omega_0 = 2) Tj
T*
(   * pi * zeta.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Relaxation Time \(tau\):) Tj
T*
(   - Relaxation time tau is defined as the time interval required for the amplitude of oscillation) Tj
T*
(   to decay to 1/e \(~ 36.8%\) of its initial value:) Tj
T*
(   exp\( - beta * tau \) = exp\( - 1 \) => tau = 1 / beta = 2 * m / b.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Quality Factor Q:) Tj
T*
(   - Quality factor Q measures the energy retention efficiency of the oscillator:) Tj
T*
(   Q = 2 * pi * \( Stored Energy \) / \( Energy Dissipated per Cycle \).) Tj
T*
(   - In terms of damping parameters:) Tj
T*
(   Q = omega_0 / \( 2 * beta \) = omega_0 * tau / 2 = pi / delta.) Tj
T*
(   - High Q indicates minimal damping and sharp resonance; low Q indicates heavy damping.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
