(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the equation of motion for a forced harmonic oscillator. Derive the steady-state amplitude and phase response, and obtain the conditions for amplitude resonance and velocity resonance.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Equation of Motion:) Tj
T*
(   - A mass m with damping b and spring stiffness k is driven by an external sinusoidal force F\(t\)) Tj
T*
(   = F_0 * cos\(omega * t\):) Tj
T*
(   m * \(d^2x / dt^2\) + b * \(dx / dt\) + k * x = F_0 * cos\(omega * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - In standard notation: d^2x / dt^2 + 2*beta * \(dx/dt\) + omega_0^2 * x = f_0 * cos\(omega * t\),) Tj
T*
(   where f_0 = F_0 / m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Steady-State Solution:) Tj
T*
(   - After transient oscillations decay, the steady-state response oscillates at driving frequency) Tj
T*
(   omega:) Tj
T*
(   x\(t\) = A\(omega\) * cos\( omega * t - phi \).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting into the differential equation and equating coefficients of cos\(omega*t\) and) Tj
T*
(   sin\(omega*t\):) Tj
T*
(   \( omega_0^2 - omega^2 \) * A = f_0 * cos\(phi\)) Tj
T*
(   2 * beta * omega * A = f_0 * sin\(phi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Squaring and adding both equations:) Tj
T*
(   A^2 * [ \(omega_0^2 - omega^2\)^2 + 4 * beta^2 * omega^2 ] = f_0^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Steady-state amplitude:) Tj
T*
(   A\(omega\) = f_0 / sqrt\( \(omega_0^2 - omega^2\)^2 + 4 * beta^2 * omega^2 \) = \(F_0 / m\) / sqrt\() Tj
T*
(   \(omega_0^2 - omega^2\)^2 + 4*beta^2*omega^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Phase lag phi:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(phi\) = \( 2 * beta * omega \) / \( omega_0^2 - omega^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Amplitude Resonance Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Amplitude A\(omega\) is maximized when the denominator function g\(omega\) = \(omega_0^2 -) Tj
T*
(   omega^2\)^2 + 4*beta^2*omega^2 is minimized.) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiating with respect to omega and setting to zero:) Tj
T*
(   d\(g\) / d\(omega\) = 2 * \(omega_0^2 - omega^2\) * \(- 2*omega\) + 8 * beta^2 * omega = 0.) Tj
T*
ET

