(   - 4 * omega * [ omega_0^2 - omega^2 - 2 * beta^2 ] = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Solving for resonant frequency omega_r:) Tj
T*
(   omega_r = sqrt\( omega_0^2 - 2 * beta^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Peak amplitude at resonance:) Tj
T*
(   A_max = f_0 / [ 2 * beta * sqrt\(omega_0^2 - beta^2\) ].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Velocity Resonance Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Velocity v\(t\) = dx/dt has amplitude v_0 = omega * A\(omega\) = f_0 / sqrt\( \(omega_0^2/omega -) Tj
T*
(   omega\)^2 + 4*beta^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - The term \(omega_0^2/omega - omega\)^2 vanishes when omega = omega_0.) Tj
T*
(   - Velocity resonance occurs exactly at the natural undamped frequency omega = omega_0, where) Tj
T*
(   velocity is in-phase with driving force \(phi = pi/2\).) Tj
