(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the civil engineering significance of mechanical resonance. Discuss the Tacoma Narrows Bridge collapse and describe the working principle of Tuned Mass Dampers \(TMD\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Resonance Hazards in Civil Infrastructure:) Tj
T*
(   - Civil structures \(tall buildings, long-span suspension bridges, chimneys, transmission) Tj
T*
(   towers\) possess intrinsic natural frequencies of vibration.) Tj
T*
(   - When periodic dynamic forces \(wind gust shedding, earthquake ground shaking, heavy traffic,) Tj
T*
(   synchronized pedestrian marching\) match a natural structural frequency, resonance occurs.) Tj
T*
(   - Amplitude escalates by dynamic amplification factor DAF ~= 1 / \(2*zeta\) \(often 20 to 50 times) Tj
T*
(   static deflection\), generating destructive stresses that cause structural collapse.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Tacoma Narrows Bridge Disaster \(November 7, 1940\):) Tj
T*
(   - A steady moderate wind of 42 mph \(68 km/h\) generated alternating Karman vortex shedding) Tj
T*
(   behind the solid plate-girder deck.) Tj
T*
(   - The vortex shedding frequency locked onto the bridge's torsional torsional resonant mode \(0.2) Tj
T*
(   Hz\).) Tj
T*
(   - Aeroelastic flutter induced violent twisting oscillations \(+- 45 degrees\), culminating in) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic deck rupture.) Tj
T*
(   - Modern aerodynamic redesign: Aerodynamic open trusses, slotted deck grates, and aerodynamic) Tj
T*
(   fairings.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Tuned Mass Dampers \(TMD\):) Tj
T*
(   - A passive structural vibration control device consisting of an auxiliary secondary mass m_d,) Tj
T*
(   spring stiffness k_d, and viscous damper c_d installed near the top of tall buildings \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Taipei 101's 660-tonne suspended steel sphere\).) Tj
T*
(   - Working Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * The TMD natural frequency is tuned precisely to match the building's fundamental swaying) Tj
T*
(   frequency: omega_d = omega_building.) Tj
T*
(   * When the building sways during typhoons or earthquakes, the TMD resonates in counter-phase) Tj
T*
(   \(180 degrees out of phase\).) Tj
T*
(   * The swinging TMD exerts an equal and opposite reaction force on the building frame,) Tj
T*
(   transferring kinetic energy to its hydraulic dampers and reducing building sway by 40% to 60%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
