(   - When a sound source radiates acoustic power inside an enclosed room, sound waves strike) Tj
T*
(   boundaries \(walls, floor, ceiling, furniture\).) Tj
T*
(   - At each boundary reflection, a fraction alpha of energy is absorbed while \(1 - alpha\) is) Tj
T*
(   reflected back into the room.) Tj
T*
(   - The sound field builds up to a steady state as energy supply balances absorption.) Tj
T*
(   - When the source is abruptly shut off, sound does not vanish instantly; it persists as a) Tj
T*
(   decaying diffuse sound field due to millions of successive reflections. This persistence of) Tj
T*
(   sound is termed Reverberation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Definition of Reverberation Time \(RT60\):) Tj
T*
(   - Formulated by Wallace Clement Sabine \(Harvard, 1898\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reverberation Time \(T or RT60\) is defined as the time interval required for the sound energy) Tj
T*
(   density in an enclosed room to drop to one-millionth \(10^-6 or -60 dB\) of its initial) Tj
T*
(   steady-state value:) Tj
T*
(   10 * log10\( I_final / I_initial \) = 10 * log10\( 10^-6 \) = - 60 dB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Sabine's Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - In metric SI units:) Tj
T*
(   T = \( 0.161 * V \) / A = \( 0.161 * V \) / \( Sum_{i=1}^N alpha_i * S_i \),) Tj
T*
(   where:) Tj
T*
(   * T = Reverberation Time in seconds \(s\).) Tj
T*
(   * V = Net internal volume of the room in cubic meters \(m^3\).) Tj
T*
(   * A = Total acoustic absorption of the room in metric Sabins \(m^2 of open window equivalent\).) Tj
T*
(   * S_i = Surface area of the i-th boundary material in square meters \(m^2\).) Tj
T*
(   * alpha_i = Acoustic absorption coefficient of the i-th surface material \(dimensionless, 0 <=) Tj
T*
(   alpha <= 1\).) Tj
T*
(   * The numerical constant 0.161 = \(24 * ln 10\) / c \(for speed of sound c = 343 m/s in air at 20) Tj
T*
(   C\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Limitations:) Tj
T*
(   - Sabine's formula assumes a perfectly diffuse sound field with uniform absorption distribution) Tj
T*
(   and moderate absorption \(alpha_avg < 0.25\). For dead rooms \(alpha_avg > 0.3\), Eyring's formula) Tj
T*
(   must be used.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
