(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive Sabine's formula for the growth and decay of sound energy density in a hall, and obtain the expression for Reverberation Time T = 0.161 * V / A.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Rate of Energy Supply and Decay Model:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider a hall of volume V and total surface area S with total absorption A = alpha_avg * S.) Tj
T*
(   - Let the sound source emit acoustic power P \(Watts\). Let average sound energy density at time) Tj
T*
(   t be E\(t\) \(J/m^3\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rate of Energy Incident on Hall Surfaces:) Tj
T*
(   - In a diffuse sound field, energy strikes walls from all directions uniformly.) Tj
T*
(   - Total sound energy incident per unit surface area per unit time is: I_incident = E * c / 4,) Tj
T*
(   where c is speed of sound.) Tj
T*
(   - Total rate of energy absorption by all room surfaces:) Tj
T*
(   Rate of absorption = I_incident * A = \( E * c / 4 \) * A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Differential Equation for Energy Density Balance:) Tj
T*
(   - Conservation of acoustic energy in volume V:) Tj
T*
(   Net rate of energy increase = Power supplied - Rate of absorption.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
