/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss common architectural acoustic defects in lecture halls, theaters, and auditoriums \(echo, flutter echo, sound focusing, dead spots\) and explain remediation measures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Acoustic Defect 1: Echoes:) Tj
T*
(   - Defect: Distinct repetition of sound heard when delayed reflection arrives > 0.07 s \(~ 17 m) Tj
T*
(   path difference\) after direct sound, confusing speech.) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Massive flat, unyielding rear walls.) Tj
T*
(   - Remediation: Cover rear walls with heavy acoustic absorbers \(fiberglass, acoustic fabric\) or) Tj
T*
(   convex polycylindrical diffusers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Acoustic Defect 2: Flutter Echoes:) Tj
T*
(   - Defect: A rapid, hollow buzzing or ringing flutter heard after impulsive sounds \(claps\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Sound trapped between two hard, smooth, parallel reflecting side walls.) Tj
T*
(   - Remediation: Splay side walls outward by >= 5 degrees \(non-parallel alignment\), or alternate) Tj
T*
(   absorption and diffusion panels along opposite walls.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Acoustic Defect 3: Sound Focusing:) Tj
T*
(   - Defect: Extreme amplification of sound at specific geometric focal points while starving) Tj
T*
(   surrounding seating areas.) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Concave ceiling domes, curved rear walls, or cylindrical prosceniums.) Tj
T*
(   - Remediation: Avoid concave interior surfaces; install convex reflective clouds \(canopies\)) Tj
T*
(   under domes, or line concave curves with deep acoustic absorptive treatment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Acoustic Defect 4: Dead Spots \(Shadow Zones\):) Tj
T*
(   - Defect: Areas where sound is faint and muffled with poor intelligibility.) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Destructive interference or acoustic shadowing under deep balcony overhangs \(where) Tj
T*
(   overhang depth D > 2 * opening height H\).) Tj
T*
(   - Remediation: Limit balcony overhang depth \(D <= 1.5 * H\); install inclined reflective ceiling) Tj
T*
(   panels above the stage to direct sound deep under balconies; add under-balcony delayed) Tj
T*
(   electroacoustic fill speakers.) Tj
T*
ET

