(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the factors governing the acoustic design of an auditorium: volume, reverberation time, shape, materials, and background noise criteria \(NC\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Hall Volume and Seating Capacity:) Tj
T*
(   - General design standard: 4.0 to 5.5 m^3 per seat for speech/theaters; 7.0 to 9.0 m^3 per seat) Tj
T*
(   for music/symphony halls.) Tj
T*
(   - Excess volume creates prolonged reverberation and muddy sound; insufficient volume produces) Tj
T*
(   cramped, dead acoustics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Target Reverberation Time \(RT60\):) Tj
T*
(   - Speech/Lecture Halls: RT60 = 0.8 to 1.1 seconds \(high clarity\).) Tj
T*
(   - Musical Concert Halls: RT60 = 1.8 to 2.2 seconds \(richness, fullness of tone, reverberant) Tj
T*
(   warmth\).) Tj
T*
(   - Multi-purpose Auditoriums: RT60 = 1.3 to 1.6 seconds \(often supplemented by active electronic) Tj
T*
(   acoustic enhancement\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Room Geometric Shape:) Tj
T*
(   - Optimum geometry: Fan-shaped with splayed walls \(10-15 degrees\) or classic shoebox hall.) Tj
T*
(   - Shoebox halls provide strong early lateral reflections \(within 50 ms\) to human ears, creating) Tj
T*
(   acoustic spaciousness and binaural envelopment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Material Selection and Distribution:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage and Proscenium: Hard sound-reflective surfaces \(dense polished hardwood, heavy gypsum) Tj
T*
(   board\) to project sound forward.) Tj
T*
(   - Rear Wall: High-absorption acoustic panels \(alpha > 0.8\) to eliminate slap-back echoes.) Tj
T*
(   - Side Walls: Mixture of sound diffusers and absorbers.) Tj
T*
(   - Seating: Fully upholstered seats whose absorption when empty matches an occupied seat \(alpha) Tj
T*
(   ~ 0.7\), ensuring RT60 remains constant regardless of audience size.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Background Noise Control \(Noise Criteria NC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Noise Criteria rating must not exceed NC-20 to NC-25.) Tj
T*
(   - HVAC air duct velocities kept < 2.5 m/s; silencers installed in ducts; mechanical plant rooms) Tj
T*
(   isolated with floating acoustic slabs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
