(   2. Experimental Apparatus and Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   - A nickel rod of length L is clamped rigidly at its center \(forming a displacement node at) Tj
T*
(   center, antinodes at free ends\).) Tj
T*
(   - Two coils are wound around the rod: a driving coil L1 in an LC electronic tank circuit, and a) Tj
T*
(   feedback coil L2 connected to the grid/gate of an amplifier tube or transistor.) Tj
T*
(   - By tuning the variable capacitor C, the electronic oscillation frequency is adjusted to match) Tj
T*
(   the natural mechanical frequency of the rod.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Resonant Frequency:) Tj
T*
(   - The rod vibrates longitudinally as a standing acoustic wave clamped at its center.) Tj
T*
(   - Length L corresponds to one half-wavelength for the fundamental mode:) Tj
T*
(   L = lambda / 2 => lambda = 2 * L.) Tj
T*
(   - The acoustic wave velocity in a solid rod is v = sqrt\( Y / rho \), where Y is Young's modulus) Tj
T*
(   and rho is material density.) Tj
T*
(   - The fundamental resonant frequency is:) Tj
T*
(   f = v / lambda = \( 1 / 2L \) * sqrt\( Y / rho \).) Tj
T*
(   - For p-th harmonic overtone: f_p = \( p / 2L \) * sqrt\( Y / rho \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Inherent Limitations:) Tj
T*
(   - Frequency Ceiling: Limited to frequencies below 100 kHz. Above 100 kHz, massive eddy current) Tj
T*
(   and magnetic hysteresis losses generate intense heat in the metal rod, causing loss of) Tj
T*
(   ferromagnetic properties \(Curie point\).) Tj
T*
(   - Narrow operational bandwidth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
