(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Piezoelectric method for generating high-frequency ultrasonics. Explain direct and inverse piezoelectric effects, draw the Hartley/Colpitts oscillator circuit, and derive the crystal resonant frequency.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Piezoelectric Effect:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Direct Piezoelectric Effect \(Curie brothers, 1880\): When mechanical stress \(compression) Tj
T*
(   or tension\) is applied along the mechanical axis of non-centrosymmetric crystals \(e.g., Quartz,) Tj
T*
(   PZT, BaTiO3\), opposite electrical charges develop on opposite faces.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Inverse \(Converse\) Piezoelectric Effect \(Lippmann, 1881\): When an external alternating) Tj
T*
(   electric voltage is applied across opposite faces of the crystal, it undergoes mechanical) Tj
T*
(   contraction and expansion at the applied frequency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Piezoelectric Oscillator Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   - An X-cut quartz crystal or PZT ceramic disc of thickness t is mounted between two lightweight) Tj
T*
(   metal plate electrodes.) Tj
T*
(   - The crystal is placed in the tuned LC tank circuit of an RF electronic oscillator \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Hartley, Colpitts, or Pierce configuration\).) Tj
T*
(   - When the electrical frequency of the LC tank circuit tuned by capacitor C matches the) Tj
T*
(   mechanical resonant frequency of the crystal slice, intense acoustic resonance occurs.) Tj
T*
(   - Millions of ultrasound waves per second are radiated into the adjacent medium.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Crystal Resonant Frequency:) Tj
T*
(   - For fundamental thickness-mode vibration, the two outer faces of the crystal plate of) Tj
T*
(   thickness t act as displacement antinodes, while the center plane is a node.) Tj
T*
(   - The thickness t equals one half-wavelength:) Tj
T*
(   t = lambda / 2 => lambda = 2 * t.) Tj
T*
(   - The velocity of longitudinal acoustic compressional waves in the crystal is v = sqrt\( Y / rho) Tj
T*
(   \), where Y is Young's modulus and rho is crystal density.) Tj
T*
(   - Fundamental thickness resonant frequency:) Tj
T*
