(   - First, the sound concrete surface pulse velocity v is established by measuring transit time) Tj
T*
(   t1 across a crack-free baseline of length 2*x \(transmitters and receivers spaced at distance x) Tj
T*
(   on either side of a chosen datum point\):) Tj
T*
(   v = 2 * x / t1 => t1 = 2 * x / v.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Measurement Across the Crack:) Tj
T*
(   - The transmitter \(T\) and receiver \(R\) are positioned symmetrically on opposite sides of the) Tj
T*
(   crack, each at distance x from the crack line \(total surface separation = 2*x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Because an open crack contains an air gap \(acoustic impedance of air is ~ 20,000 times lower) Tj
T*
(   than concrete\), ultrasonic waves cannot cross the crack directly.) Tj
T*
(   - The pulse must travel diagonally down from transmitter T to the tip of the crack \(depth d\)) Tj
T*
(   and back up to receiver R.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Geometric Path Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - The path forms two symmetrical right-angled triangles with base x and height d.) Tj
T*
(   - Distance from transmitter T to crack tip: L_1 = sqrt\( x^2 + d^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Distance from crack tip to receiver R: L_2 = sqrt\( x^2 + d^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Total acoustic travel path length: L_crack = 2 * sqrt\( x^2 + d^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - The measured transit time across the crack t2 is:) Tj
T*
(   t2 = L_crack / v = [ 2 * sqrt\( x^2 + d^2 \) ] / v.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Solving for Crack Depth d:) Tj
T*
(   - Squaring both sides: t2^2 = 4 * \( x^2 + d^2 \) / v^2 = \( 4 * x^2 / v^2 \) + \( 4 * d^2 / v^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Notice that t1 = 2*x / v => t1^2 = 4*x^2 / v^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting t1^2 into the equation:) Tj
T*
(   t2^2 = t1^2 + \( 4 * d^2 / v^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging for d^2:) Tj
T*
(   4 * d^2 / v^2 = t2^2 - t1^2 => d^2 = \( v^2 / 4 \) * \( t2^2 - t1^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute v = 2*x / t1:) Tj
T*
(   d^2 = [ \(2*x / t1\)^2 / 4 ] * \( t2^2 - t1^2 \) = \( x^2 / t1^2 \) * \( t2^2 - t1^2 \) = x^2 * [ \(t2 /) Tj
T*
(   t1\)^2 - 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Taking the square root yields the standard crack depth equation:) Tj
T*
(   d = x * sqrt\( \(t2 / t1\)^2 - 1 \). \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
