(   [Problem Statement]: A lecture hall has dimensions 20 m x 15 m x 6 m. The ceiling has area 300 m^2 \(alpha = 0.80\), walls have area 420 m^2 \(alpha = 0.05\), floor has area 300 m^2 \(alpha = 0.10\). An audience of 250 persons is present \(each adding 0.40 metric Sabins\). Calculate: \(a\) total hall volume, \(b\) total acoustic absorption, \(c\) reverberation time T. Is it acoustically acceptable for lectures?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. \(a\) Hall Volume V:) Tj
T*
(   - V = Length * Width * Height = 20 m * 15 m * 6 m = 1800 m^3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(b\) Total Acoustic Absorption A:) Tj
T*
(   - Ceiling absorption: A_ceiling = S_c * alpha_c = 300 m^2 * 0.80 = 240.0 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
(   - Wall absorption: A_walls = S_w * alpha_w = 420 m^2 * 0.05 = 21.0 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
(   - Floor absorption: A_floor = S_f * alpha_f = 300 m^2 * 0.10 = 30.0 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
(   - Audience absorption: A_audience = 250 persons * 0.40 Sabins/person = 100.0 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
(   - Total absorption A:) Tj
T*
(   A = 240.0 + 21.0 + 30.0 + 100.0 = 391.0 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(c\) Reverberation Time T \(Sabine's Formula\):) Tj
T*
(   - T = 0.161 * V / A = \( 0.161 * 1800 \) / 391.0 = 289.8 / 391.0 = 0.741 seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Acoustic Assessment:) Tj
T*
ET

