(   [Problem Statement]: In a laboratory UPV test on a cylindrical concrete core \(length L = 200 mm, diameter D = 100 mm, mass M = 3.650 kg\), the longitudinal pulse transit time is 47.6 microseconds. If Poisson's ratio is nu = 0.20, calculate: \(a\) density rho, \(b\) ultrasonic pulse velocity v_p, \(c\) dynamic Young's modulus E_d, \(d\) dynamic shear modulus G_d.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. \(a\) Density rho of Concrete Core:) Tj
T*
(   - Radius r = D / 2 = 50 mm = 0.050 m; Length L = 200 mm = 0.200 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Core volume V = pi * r^2 * L = pi * \(0.050\)^2 * 0.200 = pi * 0.0025 * 0.200 = 1.5708 x 10^-3) Tj
T*
(   m^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Density: rho = M / V = 3.650 kg / \(1.5708 x 10^-3 m^3\) = 2323.7 kg/m^3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(b\) Ultrasonic Pulse Velocity v_p:) Tj
T*
(   - Transit time: t = 47.6 microseconds = 47.6 x 10^-6 s.) Tj
T*
(   - v_p = L / t = 0.200 m / \(47.6 x 10^-6 s\) = 4201.7 m/s = 4.202 km/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(c\) Dynamic Young's Modulus E_d:) Tj
T*
(   - For a solid elastic medium, longitudinal wave speed is related to E_d by:) Tj
T*
(   v_p = sqrt\( [ E_d * \(1 - nu\) ] / [ rho * \(1 + nu\) * \(1 - 2*nu\) ] \).) Tj
T*
(   - Poisson factor for nu = 0.20:) Tj
T*
(   F\(nu\) = [ \(1 - nu\) ] / [ \(1 + nu\) * \(1 - 2*nu\) ] = \(1 - 0.20\) / [ \(1.20\) * \(1 - 0.40\) ] = 0.80) Tj
T*
(   / [ 1.20 * 0.60 ] = 0.80 / 0.72 = 1.1111.) Tj
T*
(   - v_p^2 = \( E_d * F\(nu\) \) / rho => E_d = \( rho * v_p^2 \) / F\(nu\).) Tj
T*
(   - v_p^2 = \(4201.7\)^2 = 1.7654 x 10^7 m^2/s^2.) Tj
T*
(   - E_d = \( 2323.7 * 1.7654 x 10^7 \) / 1.1111 = \( 4.1023 x 10^10 \) / 1.1111 = 3.692 x 10^10 N/m^2) Tj
T*
(   = 36.92 GPa.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(d\) Dynamic Shear Modulus G_d:) Tj
T*
(   - Elastic relation: G_d = E_d / [ 2 * \(1 + nu\) ] = 36.92 GPa / [ 2 * 1.20 ] = 36.92 / 2.40 =) Tj
T*
(   15.38 GPa.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
