(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical principles and instrumentation of Impact-Echo \(IE\) testing for measuring concrete bridge deck thickness, delamination, and void detection beneath tendon ducts.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Working Principle of Impact-Echo \(ASTM C1383\):) Tj
T*
(   - Impact-Echo is a specialized stress-wave non-destructive method for testing concrete) Tj
T*
(   structures with single-side access.) Tj
T*
(   - A small steel spherical impactor \(diameter 4 to 12 mm\) taps the concrete surface, generating) Tj
T*
(   short-duration transient stress waves \(P-waves, S-waves, and Rayleigh waves\).) Tj
T*
(   - The P-waves travel through the thickness of the member and reflect repeatedly between the) Tj
T*
(   front surface and internal acoustic boundaries \(bottom slab face, delaminations, or hollow) Tj
T*
(   tendon ducts\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Frequency Domain Signal Processing:) Tj
T*
(   - A sensitive broadband displacement transducer adjacent to the impactor records the surface) Tj
T*
(   response.) Tj
T*
(   - Fast Fourier Transform \(FFT\) converts the time-domain waveform into an amplitude spectrum.) Tj
T*
(   - Repeated reflections establish a localized standing thickness resonance peak at frequency) Tj
T*
ET

