(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Sound Transmission Loss \(TL\) and Sound Transmission Class \(STC\) of architectural walls. State the Mass Law and describe how double-leaf cavity walls achieve high acoustic isolation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Sound Transmission Loss \(TL\):) Tj
T*
(   - When airborne sound strikes a wall partition, Sound Transmission Loss \(TL\) measures the) Tj
T*
(   acoustic power attenuation provided by the barrier:) Tj
T*
(   TL = 10 * log10\( W_incident / W_transmitted \) \(dB\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Acoustic Mass Law for Single-Leaf Partitions:) Tj
T*
(   - For a limp, single solid panel of surface mass density m \(kg/m^2\) subjected to sound of) Tj
T*
(   frequency f \(Hz\):) Tj
T*
(   TL ~= 20 * log10\( m * f \) - 48 \(dB\).) Tj
T*
(   - Rules of Thumb:) Tj
T*
(   * Doubling the surface mass density m increases TL by ~ 6 dB.) Tj
T*
(   * Doubling the acoustic frequency f increases TL by ~ 6 dB.) Tj
T*
(   - Drawback: Achieving high sound isolation with single solid walls requires impractically) Tj
T*
(   thick, heavy concrete \(e.g., a 20 cm solid concrete wall weighs 480 kg/m^2 for STC 55\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. High-Performance Double-Leaf Cavity Walls:) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Two independent lightweight gypsum or masonry leaves separated by an air cavity) Tj
T*
(   \(depth d ~ 50 to 100 mm\) containing mineral wool acoustic insulation.) Tj
T*
(   - Mass-Air-Mass Resonance \(f_MAM\):) Tj
T*
(   f_MAM = \(1 / 2*pi\) * sqrt\( \(rho_air * c^2 / d\) * \(1/m1 + 1/m2\) \).) Tj
T*
(   - Above the mass-air-mass resonance frequency, the transmission loss increases at an) Tj
T*
(   extraordinary rate of ~ 18 dB per octave!) Tj
T*
(   - A lightweight double stud wall weighing only 50 kg/m^2 easily achieves STC 60, vastly) Tj
T*
(   outperforming a solid concrete wall ten times heavier.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
