(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the ultrasonic Phased Array Ultrasonic Testing \(PAUT\) technology and describe its advantages over conventional single-element probes for inspecting steel bridge welds.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Phased Array Ultrasonics \(PAUT\):) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike conventional NDT which uses a single piezoelectric crystal generating a fixed acoustic) Tj
T*
(   beam, a PAUT probe contains an array of numerous tiny piezoelectric elements \(typically 16 to) Tj
T*
(   128 elements\).) Tj
T*
(   - Each element is pulsed independently by software-controlled electronic time delays \(focal) Tj
T*
(   laws\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Beam Steering and Dynamic Focusing:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Electronic Beam Steering: By applying linear progressive time delays across elements, the) Tj
T*
(   acoustic wavefront is steered through angles from 35 to 75 degrees without physically moving) Tj
T*
(   the probe.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Dynamic Depth Focusing: By applying parabolic time delays, the beam is focused sharply at) Tj
T*
(   any desired depth within the structural steel weld.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Imaging Displays:) Tj
T*
(   - S-Scan \(Sectorial Scan\): Sweeps the beam through a fan of angles, generating a true) Tj
T*
(   cross-sectional slice of the weld in real time.) Tj
T*
(   - C-Scan: Top-down plan view of defect locations along the weld length.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Advantages in Structural Steel Inspection:) Tj
T*
(   - 100% volumetric weld coverage in a single line pass.) Tj
T*
(   - Exceptional sensitivity in detecting lack of side-wall fusion, incomplete penetration,) Tj
T*
(   porosity clusters, and toe micro-cracks.) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates hazardous gamma-ray radiographic testing \(RT\) on active bridge construction sites.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
