(   - Intensity reflection coefficient: R = [ \(Z2 - Z1\) / \(Z2 + Z1\) ]^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Intensity transmission coefficient: T = \( 4 * Z1 * Z2 \) / \( Z2 + Z1 \)^2 = 1 - R.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(a\) Water \(Z1\) into Concrete \(Z2\):) Tj
T*
(   - Z2 - Z1 = 9.60x10^6 - 1.48x10^6 = 8.12 x 10^6 Rayls.) Tj
T*
(   - Z2 + Z1 = 9.60x10^6 + 1.48x10^6 = 11.08 x 10^6 Rayls.) Tj
T*
(   - R_wc = \( 8.12 / 11.08 \)^2 = \( 0.7328 \)^2 = 0.537 = 53.7%.) Tj
T*
(   - T_wc = 1 - 0.537 = 0.463 = 46.3%.) Tj
T*
(   - Water provides fair acoustic coupling \(46.3% energy transmits into concrete\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(b\) Concrete \(Z1\) into Air \(Z2\):) Tj
T*
(   - Z2 - Z1 = 408 - 9.60x10^6 ~= - 9.60 x 10^6 Rayls.) Tj
T*
(   - Z2 + Z1 = 408 + 9.60x10^6 ~= 9.60 x 10^6 Rayls.) Tj
T*
(   - R_ca = [ \(408 - 9.6x10^6\) / \(408 + 9.6x10^6\) ]^2 ~= \( - 0.999915 \)^2 = 0.99983 = 99.983%.) Tj
T*
(   - T_ca = \( 4 * 9.6x10^6 * 408 \) / \(9.6x10^6\)^2 = 1.567x10^10 / 9.216x10^13 = 1.70 x 10^-4 =) Tj
T*
(   0.017%.) Tj
T*
(   - 99.98% of ultrasound energy reflects at a concrete-air boundary, explaining why even) Tj
T*
(   microscopic cracks create total signal blockage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 22:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Cross-Hole Sonic Logging \(CSL\) method for testing deep foundation drilled shafts \(bored concrete piles\). Describe testing procedure, data interpretation, and defect identification.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose of CSL Testing \(ASTM D6760\):) Tj
T*
(   - Drilled shafts \(bored piles\) carry immense structural loads for bridge piers and skyscrapers,) Tj
T*
(   penetrating 20 to 60 meters underground.) Tj
T*
(   - Deep casting under bentonite slurry often suffers from concrete soil contamination, necking,) Tj
T*
(   honeycombing, or soft pile toes.) Tj
T*
(   - CSL provides rigorous cross-sectional integrity evaluation between pairs of vertical access) Tj
T*
(   tubes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Equipment and Setup:) Tj
T*
(   - During rebar cage fabrication, 2 to 6 steel or PVC tubes \(diameter ~ 50 mm\) are tied) Tj
T*
(   vertically along the entire length of the cage and filled with water.) Tj
T*
(   - An ultrasonic transmitter probe is lowered down one tube, and a receiver probe down another) Tj
T*
(   tube.) Tj
T*
(   - A depth encoder synchronizes the automated motorized retrieval of both probes simultaneously) Tj
T*
(   from bottom to top at speed ~ 0.3 m/s, recording ultrasound pulses every 50 mm of depth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Data Interpretation and Defect Signatures:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Sound Concrete: Displays constant First Arrival Time \(FAT\) corresponding to v_p ~ 3800 to) Tj
T*
(   4200 m/s with strong signal energy amplitude.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Moderate Flaw: FAT increases by 10% to 20% with 6 to 9 dB energy loss, indicating) Tj
T*
(   localized porous concrete.) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) Severe Defect: FAT delay > 20% accompanied by > 20 dB signal energy drop \(or complete) Tj
T*
(   signal loss\), indicating soil intrusion, void voids, or necking.) Tj
T*
(   - Tomographic 2D/3D inversion reconstructs the exact spatial boundary of the defect, guiding) Tj
T*
(   high-pressure permeation grouting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
