(   [Problem Statement]: A multi-purpose school hall of volume 4000 m^3 has a reverberation time of 2.2 seconds. It is desired to lower the reverberation time to 1.1 seconds for speech clarity. Calculate the additional absorption required in metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Room volume: V = 4000 m^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Initial reverberation time: T1 = 2.20 seconds.) Tj
T*
(   - Target reverberation time: T2 = 1.10 seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Initial Total Absorption A1 \(Sabine's Formula\):) Tj
T*
(   - T1 = 0.161 * V / A1 => A1 = 0.161 * V / T1.) Tj
T*
(   - A1 = \( 0.161 * 4000 \) / 2.20 = 644.0 / 2.20 = 292.73 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Target Total Absorption A2:) Tj
T*
(   - T2 = 0.161 * V / A2 => A2 = 0.161 * V / T2.) Tj
T*
(   - A2 = \( 0.161 * 4000 \) / 1.10 = 644.0 / 1.10 = 585.45 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Additional Absorption Required Delta_A:) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_A = A2 - A1 = 585.45 - 292.73 = 292.72 metric Sabins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Architectural Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   - If acoustic fabric-wrapped mineral wool panels with alpha = 0.85 are installed on walls:) Tj
T*
(   Required panel area = Delta_A / alpha = 292.72 / 0.85 = 344.4 m^2 of wall coverage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 26:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical principles and applications of the Spectral Analysis of Surface Waves \(SASW\) and Multi-Channel Analysis of Surface Waves \(MASW\) in geotechnical and highway pavement engineering.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Principles of Surface Wave Dispersion:) Tj
T*
(   - When an impact source \(sledgehammer or drop weight\) strikes the ground surface, ~ 67% of) Tj
T*
(   total seismic energy propagates as Rayleigh \(R\) surface waves.) Tj
T*
(   - In a vertically layered medium \(e.g., asphalt over granular base over soil subgrade\),) Tj
T*
(   Rayleigh waves are dispersive: different frequency components travel at different phase) Tj
T*
(   velocities.) Tj
T*
(   - High-frequency \(short wavelength\) waves sample shallow surface layers; low-frequency \(long) Tj
T*
(   wavelength\) waves penetrate deeply into subgrade soil.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. MASW Testing Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - A linear array of 12 to 48 low-frequency geophones \(4.5 Hz\) is spaced along the ground.) Tj
T*
(   - A sledgehammer impact triggers multichannel wave recording.) Tj
T*
(   - Wavefield transformation \(phase-shift or f-k transform\) extracts the experimental dispersion) Tj
T*
(   curve: Phase Velocity v_R vs Frequency f.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Inversion to Shear Wave Velocity Profile:) Tj
T*
(   - Numerical inversion algorithms calculate the 1D/2D shear wave velocity profile v_s\(z\) with) Tj
T*
(   depth.) Tj
T*
(   - Small-strain shear modulus G_max is determined: G_max = rho * v_s^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - Seismic Site Classification \(V_s30\) for earthquake building codes.) Tj
T*
(   - Non-destructive stiffness profiling of pavement layers without coring.) Tj
T*
(   - Detecting subterranean sinkholes, buried utilities, and abandoned mine shafts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

